{"name":"Gizmo","hex":"#d4a1b5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gizmo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something, generally a device or gadget, whose real name is unknown or forgotten."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gizmo"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Gizmo","blocks":[{"text":"The Gizmotron, originally developed and called the Gizmo, is an effects device for the electric guitar and bass guitar. It was invented in 1969 and patented in 1975 by the English rock musicians Kevin Godley and Lol Creme of the British rock group 10cc."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Gizmo","wikidata":"Q3108224"},{"title":"Gizmo key","blocks":[{"text":"The gizmo key is a key commonly found on the B foot joint of certain models of flute. It closes the low B tone hole without closing the low C tone hole or the low C♯ tone hole, which is intended to facilitate the performance of the fourth octave C."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gizmo_key","wikidata":"Q5565934"},{"title":"Gizmo (DC Comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Gizmo is the name of two fictional characters appearing in American comic books published by DC Comics, primarily as an enemy of the Teen Titans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d1/Gizmo_%28DC_Comics_character%29.jpg/330px-Gizmo_%28DC_Comics_character%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gizmo_(DC_Comics)","wikidata":"Q7878182"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2e/Gizmo_Teen_Titans_Go%21.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2e/Gizmo_Teen_Titans_Go%21.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Gizmo as he appears in Teen Titans Go! (2013).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGizmo_Teen_Titans_Go!.jpeg"}],"sounds":{"gizm